Update: I emailed their company, told them my problem, they answered lighting fast, less than an hour, after trying their fix, it worked.
Now I can say the game is awesome again, sad as♥♥♥♥♥maybe, sure, but im loving it.
what happened: my guy died, i was heartbroken so i tried to close the game with task manage
hoping it wouldnt save. it seems that doing so corrupted the save file and now the game would crash on startup. Basically had to erase the save file while offline and that fixed it, heres their email for reference. the second option is what worked.
- make sure that Steam is in offline mode (this will prevent the game from downloading the broken save from the Steam Cloud);
- go to folder: (wherever you have Steam Installed)\Steam\userdata\YOUR-PROFILE-ID-NUMBER\282070\remote (For me it's C:\Apps\Steam\userdata\7XXXXX1\282070\remote);
- delete/rename/move the "savedgames" file;
- change the "savedgames.alt" file name to "savedgames";
- launch the game and click "continue";
- your game should load the state from the previous day.
If this fails as well, please go to the folder at "%appdata%/11bitstudios/This War of Mine" (you can simply copy the directory and paste it into the adress bar in Explorer) and delete the "iPhoneProfiles" file. This is the file that records beginning and end of each session - the end of session is recorded when the game is closed via choosing the appropriate option from the menu in-game, and unexpected shutdown of the game may cause the session end not to be recorded, which leads to an error within Steam upon next launch. Please delete the file and try to launch the game again.

