As you can tell from my time played-this is a first impressions review based on my own experience so far and research. The staff  really love this game-and continued to work on it even when they weren't getting paid... Microsoft kinda mesed them up further by making them sign an exclusive contract. The gameplay is really fun! It's unique, great artstyle,smooth,etc! It's a great game that just needs love and money/popularity.
for cons: The UI isn't great...but it's a WIP i guess... the matchmaking sucks due to the low popularity. (I really dont like the arc client)
Overall this is a really fun and pretty unique game that I would love to see gain popularity so it can thrive...it has lots of potential.

What happens when you take World of Goo and combine it with Bridge Builder?! Well, you get Tiny Bridge Ratventure. The basic premise of the game is to traverse 2 rats through a hostile terrain by building structures to collect cheese. The main principal of this physics basic bridge builder is nothing new as there are a lot of these type of games on the market but Ratventure does offer a few different mechanics that set it asside from the rest. Regardless of Ratventures small amount originalities, they still do not justify a $10.99 price point. My recommendation is only to buy it on sale (
).
Lets look at the good (
), the bad (
), and the ugly (straight-up "
").
is that I am partial to these physics based bridge builder type games. The developer Estelion added player semi-controlled mechanics (opposed to automated as most bridge builder games are but movement is limited to points on the structure) making traversing the structure a little more difficult with hazards on the map. To add to the difficulty, they've added bonus cheese for extra points in addition to the level ending big cheese. The non-player controlled mechanics (I want to call these sprites "enemies" but they both help and hinder progress, so we will label them as "NPC's") have both positive and negative affects on your structure, sometimes making it bounce and sway, or adding stability to a structure. Building on to your structure while while its swaying all over the screen adds a challenge as well as a lot more teadium to the time it takes to build. Though you are limited to only building strut parts to your structure, in addition to the NPC's there are added variables for your bridge in the maps. These include ancor points and rope suspenders, both of which you have little to no placement control over.
is that there are a lot of these games to choose from. Most of which at the same price point (not on sale) offer better graphics, better sound, more gameplay options or are just cheaper. Next, the only instruction for the game is pictures... Yes, there is not one word written for this game. Though it easy is to pick up, you still have to figure out how to play this game through the cryptic picture instructions given to you at the begining; and even then, there is no explanation of what everything does. Regardless, there is always trial and error or the community hub... Good luck there! I have not confirmed this but it is apparent with the game play that Ratventure is likely ported from either Andriod or iOS formats (couldn't find this one on the Google market) the bad part about it is that the games porting was never updated for the PC. This becomes more apparent with the instructions telling you to use your finger with the game mechanics.
part of the bad is that while the graphics are only okay, there are 6 worlds, each are just reskinned repeats of the last, and they never offer additional mechanics to differenciate it from it from the others. The first bit of ugliness most will notice is the lack of menu options. The only options that are available are play, a link to the dev's website, instructions (or lack there-of), and mute - which is not a bad thing as both the sound and music are absolutely horendous. Make sure you have a decent playlist ready before you start playing. Lastly with the options (again... or lack there-of), there is no full screen (...or any other graphic options for that matter), no control options, not even an exit... wow. Estelion developers please note this article on
The verdict for gamers is to avoid it if your not into the gameplay and buy it on sale!
